### Paragraph 2

Children in Contact with the Law

#### Article 36

1. Special Protection for Children in Contact with the Law as referred to in Article 32 paragraph (1) letter b shall be carried out through:
   a. humane treatment with attention to needs according to their age;  
   b. separation from adults;  
   c. provision of legal aid and other assistance effectively;  
   d. implementation of recreational activities;  
   e. freedom from torture, punishment, or other treatment that is cruel, inhumane, and degrading to dignity and degree;  
   f. avoidance of imposition of death penalty and/or life imprisonment;  
   g. avoidance of arrest, detention or imprisonment, except as a last resort and for the shortest possible time;  
   h. provision of a hearing/trial before a Children's court that is objective, impartial, and in a closed session to the public;  
   i. avoidance of publication of their identity;  
   j. provision of accompaniment by parents/guardians and persons trusted by the Child;  
